15:51.933 --> 15:54.601
I find it cleanses
the immeasurable sadness

15:54.669 --> 15:56.535
of having lain with a wretch.

15:56.603 --> 15:57.770
I want a divorce!

15:57.838 --> 15:59.238
You got it!

15:59.306 --> 16:01.273
Sorry. I opened
some of the gifts.

16:08.580 --> 16:10.847
Does the Swanson divorce
mean that I

16:10.915 --> 16:12.548
have to go live
with Grandma and Grandpa?

16:12.616 --> 16:14.317
No, Chris, it does not.

16:14.384 --> 16:15.885
That doesn't even
make any sense.

16:15.953 --> 16:17.285
Peter, I can't believe

16:17.353 --> 16:19.271
you would encourage Joe
to have an affair.

16:19.338 --> 16:20.721
Look, Lois, it's
in the Bible.

16:20.789 --> 16:22.156
What's in the Bible?

16:22.224 --> 16:23.524
I-I don't know.

16:23.592 --> 16:25.325
Doesn't that always
cover it somehow?

16:25.392 --> 16:27.060
Peter, you blew up
their marriage.

16:27.127 --> 16:28.961
This was
a huge mistake.

16:29.028 --> 16:30.495
Well, we've all made mistakes.

16:33.348 --> 16:34.999
Eh.

16:36.685 --> 16:38.535
(Stewie screaming)

16:38.603 --> 16:40.854
Why did the sign say
"not an exit"?

16:40.922 --> 16:43.022
It should have just said
"gorilla door."

16:43.089 --> 16:44.406
(screaming)

16:47.676 --> 16:49.726
So, it's really
over, huh?

16:49.794 --> 16:51.361
After all
these years?

16:51.429 --> 16:52.629
I'm afraid so.

16:52.697 --> 16:54.063
But let's be
honest, Peter.

16:54.131 --> 16:56.232
Bonnie and I seem
to have grown apart.

16:56.300 --> 16:57.566
Boy, I never would have seen

16:57.633 --> 16:59.417
this day coming
when we first met.

16:59.485 --> 17:02.486
"Africa" by Toto was playing.

17:02.537 --> 17:05.039
♪ ♪

17:07.074 --> 17:10.409
♪ I hear the drums
echoing tonight ♪

17:10.493 --> 17:12.744
♪ But she hears only whispers ♪

17:12.829 --> 17:16.731
♪ Of some quiet conversation ♪

17:19.383 --> 17:22.718
♪ I stopped an old man
along the way ♪

17:22.802 --> 17:25.871
♪ Hoping to find
some long forgotten words ♪

17:25.922 --> 17:29.540
♪ Or ancient melodies ♪

17:29.591 --> 17:33.510
♪ He turned to me as if to say ♪

17:33.561 --> 17:38.097
♪ "Hurry, boy,
it's waiting there for you" ♪

17:40.933 --> 17:45.936
♪ It's gonna take a lot
to drag me away from you ♪

17:46.021 --> 17:51.324
♪ There's nothing that a hundred
men or more could ever do ♪

17:51.391 --> 17:56.661
♪ I bless the rains
down in Africa ♪

17:56.728 --> 18:02.415
♪ Gonna take some time
to do the things we never had ♪

18:02.500 --> 18:04.583
♪ Ooh, ooh... ♪

18:13.624 --> 18:14.975
Lois, I know
how to get

18:15.043 --> 18:16.509
Joe and Bonnie
back together.

18:16.576 --> 18:18.411
Joe just told me
how he and Bonnie met.

18:18.478 --> 18:20.829
So I figure, all we got to do
is find a way

18:20.896 --> 18:22.464
to recreate the magic
of that night.

18:22.548 --> 18:23.748
Well, we better
do something soon,

18:23.816 --> 18:25.015
'cause I just
talked to Bonnie

18:25.083 --> 18:26.533
and she's already
on D-Date.

18:26.601 --> 18:28.102
What the hell's D-Date?

18:28.169 --> 18:29.602
Diarrhea Date.
It's filthy.

18:29.687 --> 18:31.120
But she found someone,

18:31.188 --> 18:33.021
and they're doing whatever
they do tomorrow.

18:33.089 --> 18:35.357
What the hell's
wrong with people?

18:37.092 --> 18:38.826
Thanks for inviting
me to lunch, Lois,

18:38.894 --> 18:40.861
but why are we eating
at a strip club?

18:40.929 --> 18:43.163
I know the waitress here
from water aerobics.

18:43.230 --> 18:45.098
She said she'd
give us 20% off.

18:46.566 --> 18:48.433
All units, all units.

18:48.485 --> 18:50.234
We have a disturbance
at the Fuzzy Clam.

18:50.285 --> 18:51.402
This is Officer Swanson.

18:51.453 --> 18:52.787
What's the problem?

18:52.871 --> 18:55.038
Well, one of the dancers
was dancing with a guy

18:55.106 --> 18:57.157
and saying, "You're my favorite,
you're my favorite,"

18:57.241 --> 18:58.908
but now she's dancing
with another guy.

18:58.959 --> 19:00.292
That's not a crime.

19:00.377 --> 19:01.793
Well, shouldn't it be?

19:01.877 --> 19:03.277
I'll be right there.

19:03.329 --> 19:05.430
(siren whooping)

19:07.382 --> 19:09.650
("Africa" by Toto playing)

19:09.718 --> 19:12.835
Boy, I haven't heard this
song in a long time.

19:12.920 --> 19:14.803
Police! What's going on?

19:14.887 --> 19:16.655
Bonnie?

19:16.723 --> 19:17.956
Joe?

19:18.007 --> 19:19.140
What are you
doing here?

19:19.224 --> 19:20.307
I'm here with Lois.

19:20.392 --> 19:21.726
What are you doing here?

19:21.793 --> 19:23.593
I got a call.

19:23.644 --> 19:26.312
Is that... is that
"Africa" by Toto?

19:26.397 --> 19:27.796
Yeah.

19:27.847 --> 19:29.314
That's our song.

19:29.382 --> 19:30.932
It is.

19:30.983 --> 19:35.352
♪ But she hears only whispers
of some quiet... ♪

19:35.436 --> 19:37.771
Well, it seems like
things are fine here.

19:37.822 --> 19:39.822
Listen, Bonnie,
I, uh...

19:39.906 --> 19:41.907
I just want to
say I'm sorry.

19:41.975 --> 19:44.642
I was a real ass,
and I miss you.

19:44.693 --> 19:46.444
I'm sorry, too.

19:46.495 --> 19:49.613
I know I haven't been
that easy to live with lately.

19:49.664 --> 19:52.281
Okay.

19:52.332 --> 19:55.334
Well, I'm going
to go now.

19:55.419 --> 19:58.336
Joe, wait.

19:58.421 --> 20:01.205
You want a lap dance, mister?

20:03.341 --> 20:05.491
No. Sit down.

20:05.543 --> 20:07.761
I'm giving you one.

20:07.828 --> 20:11.496
♪ The wild dogs
cry out in the night ♪

20:11.548 --> 20:13.347
♪ As they grow restless ♪

20:13.432 --> 20:17.934
♪ Longing for
some solitary company ♪

20:19.771 --> 20:20.886
Oh, Joe.

20:20.971 --> 20:22.555
Oh, Bonnie.

20:22.639 --> 20:25.356
♪ He turned to me
as if to say... ♪

20:25.441 --> 20:27.225
Can you ever
forgive me?

20:27.309 --> 20:29.009
It's going to take
some time, Joe.

20:29.060 --> 20:31.145
Rest of your life okay?

20:32.863 --> 20:37.899
♪ It's gonna take a lot
to drag me away from you ♪

20:37.984 --> 20:43.037
♪ There's nothing that a hundred
men or more could ever do ♪

20:43.121 --> 20:46.539
♪ I bless the rains
down in Africa... ♪

20:46.540 --> 21:47.540
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru